{% set local_problem %}
<p>Many Brownsboro homes have been standing for generations — that's years for water to damage fascia boards. When gutters leak or overflow, water soaks into wood and causes rot that spreads if not addressed.</p>

<p>Older homes often have original fascia that's been repainted over damage rather than properly repaired. That hidden rot affects gutter attachment and can spread to structural elements.</p>

<p>We see this regularly: homes that need gutters, but first need fascia repaired so those gutters have something solid to attach to.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>We start with careful inspection, checking fascia and soffit for water damage, soft spots, and rot.</p>

<p>For damaged sections, we remove existing gutters, cut out bad wood, and install new fascia using quality materials appropriate for your home.</p>

<p>Then we install new gutters on the solid foundation.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've been repairing fascia on Brownsboro homes for over 20 years. We understand older construction and know how to match materials.</p>

<p>Our crews handle both carpentry and gutters — one company, one warranty.</p>
{% endset %}

